"The Grove of the Thoughtful is the House of Healing of the mind healer Yenu-pezth, near Vethedya."
"It is traditionally reached by teleport to the capital, then a narrow unsigned road past fields."
"Its own humbler gray alcove is in a small house by a wooden cow-pasture gate on that road."
"Patients carry green sea-glass stones down the road and set them in the soil in her honor."
"The building curves like a boat sailing through treetops, in a grove of papery-barked trees."
"A path of milky green stones leads to softly lit, gently humming hallways."
"Some healers and extended-stay patients live on the grounds."
"A larger building in the woods houses people who can't be healed or safely live alone."
"Behind it, hidden by illusions, an archway of two trees opens onto the inward path."
"The inward path is a maze of deep, curving corridors dug into the ground and open to the sky."
"Its walls hold glass shapes, vine curtains, knobby puzzle patterns and stone grottoes."
"Patients 'steep' in small grottoes lined with foggy green stone, with clear pools of water."
"Stuart saw Yenu-pezth as a child; Alden is her first human patient."
"Its alcove opens on a receiving room of pale green tiles with tall cabinets."
"The treatment room's ceiling is woven fallen branches hung with spell ingredients."
"Its bed sits frameless beneath a gap in the branches."
"The inward path's weight lets only truths worthy of it be spoken, and opens the mind to change."
"A greeting house at the head of the road lets travelers cleanse and speak honesties first."
"Stuart dedicated a new greeting house there, with a diamond floor of dark woods and amber rafters."
"It has a ritual cleansing room, a scented-smoke hearth and a small gray teleport alcove."
"A bucket of pebbles by the inward path holds offerings; a dark grove lies behind its spiral."
